guide forever/legacy/legacy-challenges
title Legacy Challenges
category Legacy
levels 1-60
zone Burning Steppes

# A planner for Forever's 65 Legacy Challenges, one step per category group.
# Source: Blizzard's "Get to Know the World of Warcraft: Forever Legacy System"
# news post. Each challenge is worth 1 account-wide Legacy Point:
#   Classes (27)     every class reaching 25, 45 and 60
#   Tradeskills (18) Alchemy, Blacksmithing, Enchanting, Engineering,
#                    Leatherworking, Tailoring reaching 150, 225 and 300
#   PvP (12)         ranks 3, 7, 10, 13, 14; Exalted with the four
#                    battleground factions (Warsong Gulch, Arathi Basin,
#                    Alterac Valley and Forever's Darkspear Islands); Field of
#                    Honor weeks 4, 7, 10
#   Adventure (2)    explore the entire world map on one character; the Lord
#                    Valthalak dungeon-set questline
#   Dungeons (3)     final boss of every level 15-25, 26-45, 46-60 dungeon
#   Raids (3)        Onyxia; all 13 Hyjal Summit bosses; all 8 Barrow Deeps
#                    bosses
# Blizzard's raid overview (October 2026): Barrow Deeps (10 players), Hyjal
# Summit (20) and Onyxia's Lair (40) open on 9 December; every Onyxia raider
# carries the Drakefire Amulet.
#
# Tracking today: what this character can prove is tracked automatically
# (level, skill rank, battleground reputation, the Valthalak quests). Everything
# else is a manual check-off: PvP ranks, Field of Honor weeks and dungeon/raid
# bosses (`kill` with no quest is a checkbox), and world exploration (notes;
# the Exploration guides track it area by area).
#
# Under the hood Legacy Challenges are achievements, but no achievement ids
# exist in our data yet (the newest wow_classic_era client tables on wago.tools
# carry none). Once a player runs `/psrec legacy` in Polestar_Recorder on a live
# Forever client and that recording is imported, every manual goal here becomes
# an `achieve <id> "Name"` goal (with `criteria <n>` for per-boss and
# per-dungeon parts) and is tracked automatically, account-wide.
#
# ASSUMED: the dungeons of each bracket are the Legacy panel's lists as two
# independent beta write-ups copy them (Novice, Experienced and Master
# Spelunker: Ragefire Chasm or Hall of Thanes; Blackfathom Deeps in 26-45; the
# Stockade in none; Razorfen Downs and Uldaman in 46-60; Forever's Drowned City,
# Krol'dok Stronghold, Alcaz Prison, Blackmaw Hold and Shaper's Terrace). Blizzard
# published only the level bands. The final boss is the last of the dungeon's
# bosses in Forever's dungeon journal (Bazzalan in Ragefire Chasm, Viktor the
# Vile in the Ruins of Lordaeron). In-game check: the Legacy panel's three
# dungeon challenges.
# ASSUMED: the Valthalak challenge runs from An Earnest Proposition to your
# class's Saving the Best for Last (the challenge text as two beta write-ups
# copy it). In-game check: the Legacy panel.
# The Drowned City, Krol'dok Stronghold, Alcaz Prison, Blackmaw Hold and the
# Shaper's Terrace are not in our dungeon data yet, so they are named-only
# checkboxes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Classes

step Classes: level 25
  tip Classes give 27 points: every class reaching 25, 45 and 60. They count once per class across your account, so a second character of a class you already raised adds nothing; a new class does. The first character to reach 25 usually unlocks the Legacy System itself.
  level 25

step Classes: level 45
  tip Level 45 with this character's class.
  level 45

step Classes: level 60
  tip Level 60 with this character's class.
  level 60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tradeskills

step Tradeskills: Alchemy
  tip Each crafting profession gives 3 points, at 150, 225 and 300. Ranks count once per profession across your account. Follow the Polestar guide "Alchemy 1-300" (Professions). A crafting profession at 150 also unlocks the Legacy System.
  skill Alchemy 150
  skill Alchemy 225
  skill Alchemy 300

step Tradeskills: Blacksmithing
  tip Follow the Polestar guide "Blacksmithing 1-300" (Professions).
  skill Blacksmithing 150
  skill Blacksmithing 225
  skill Blacksmithing 300

step Tradeskills: Enchanting
  tip Follow the Polestar guide "Enchanting 1-300" (Professions).
  skill Enchanting 150
  skill Enchanting 225
  skill Enchanting 300

step Tradeskills: Engineering
  tip Follow the Polestar guide "Engineering 1-300" (Professions).
  skill Engineering 150
  skill Engineering 225
  skill Engineering 300

step Tradeskills: Leatherworking
  tip Follow the Polestar guide "Leatherworking 1-300" (Professions).
  skill Leatherworking 150
  skill Leatherworking 225
  skill Leatherworking 300

step Tradeskills: Tailoring
  tip Follow the Polestar guide "Tailoring 1-300" (Professions).
  skill Tailoring 150
  skill Tailoring 225
  skill Tailoring 300

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- PvP

step PvP: battleground reputations (Alliance)
  only Alliance
  tip Exalted with each of the four battleground factions is worth a point. Follow the Polestar Reputation guides Warsong Gulch Reputation, Arathi Basin Reputation, Alterac Valley Reputation and Darkspear Islands Reputation (Forever's new battleground, open from level 30). The Diplomat Legacy perk increases reputation gains.
  rep 890 Exalted             -- Warsong Gulch
  rep 509 Exalted             -- Arathi Basin
  rep 730 Exalted             -- Alterac Valley
  rep 2799 Exalted            -- Darkspear Islands: Theramore Expeditionary Force

step PvP: battleground reputations (Horde)
  only Horde
  tip Exalted with each of the four battleground factions is worth a point. Follow the Polestar Reputation guides Warsong Gulch Reputation, Arathi Basin Reputation, Alterac Valley Reputation and Darkspear Islands Reputation (Forever's new battleground, open from level 30). The Diplomat Legacy perk increases reputation gains.
  rep 889 Exalted             -- Warsong Gulch
  rep 510 Exalted             -- Arathi Basin
  rep 729 Exalted             -- Alterac Valley
  rep 2798 Exalted            -- Darkspear Islands: Darkspear Raiders

step PvP: honor ranks
  tip Ranks 3, 7, 10, 13 and 14 are a point each. Polestar cannot read your highest rank yet, so tick each one off yourself. Forever's honor rules for reaching a rank have not been published in detail; in Classic, ranks come from your weekly honor standing, and 13-14 take many weeks of top standing.
  kill "enemy players for honor until PvP Rank 3"
  kill "enemy players for honor until PvP Rank 7"
  kill "enemy players for honor until PvP Rank 10"
  kill "enemy players for honor until PvP Rank 13"
  kill "enemy players for honor until PvP Rank 14"

step PvP: Field of Honor
  tip The Field of Honor PvP season has weekly journey quests; finishing the ones for weeks 4, 7 and 10 is a point each. These quests are new in Forever and not in our data, so tick each one off yourself.
  kill "enemy players and finish the Field of Honor week 4 journey quest"
  kill "enemy players and finish the Field of Honor week 7 journey quest"
  kill "enemy players and finish the Field of Honor week 10 journey quest"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Adventure

step Adventure: explore the world map
  tip Exploring the entire world map on one character is a point, and it can also unlock the Legacy System. It must all be on the same character. Forever's new zones are part of the map: the Riverglades, Shen'dralas and Mount Hyjal, a level 60 zone.
  note Follow the Polestar Exploration guides: Exploration: Eastern Kingdoms 1-30, 30-45 and 45-60, and Exploration: Kalimdor 1-30, 30-45 and 45-60. They track every area as you discover it. Exploration: Zephras Isle covers the Skyborne island; whether its map counts towards this challenge is not confirmed yet.
  note This step cannot check the whole map by itself yet; it becomes a tracked goal once the Legacy achievement ids are recorded.

step Adventure: Lord Valthalak
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip The Lord Valthalak questline is a point. It is the level 60 dungeon-set chain, from An Earnest Proposition to your class's Saving the Best for Last: Deliana (Ironforge) or Mokvar (Orgrimmar) send you through In Search of Anthion and Anthion's Parting Words to Bodley at Blackrock Mountain, whose Three Kings of Flame, the Left and Right Pieces of Lord Valthalak's Amulet, Final Preparations and Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak end with Return to Bodley. Back to the Beginning then leads to Saving the Best for Last.
  accept 8996 optional @32.2,25.8    -- Spirit of Lord Valthalak, inside Upper Blackrock Spire after Mea Culpa (no spawn in the data: the arrow leads to Bodley's Blackrock Mountain)
  turnin 8996 optional               -- Bodley: Return to Bodley
  accept 8997 only Alliance optional -- Bodley offers it once Return to Bodley is turned in
  accept 8998 only Horde optional    -- Bodley offers it once Return to Bodley is turned in

